# Template for your local settings. The setup script copies this file to
# .env.local, and that copy is where your real keys go. Never put real keys in
# this file: unlike .env.local, it gets shared along with the project.
# After changing .env.local, stop the app (Ctrl+C) and run `yarn dev` again.

# Required: your Anthropic key, which lets the app use Claude.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Prefer OpenAI? Leave the Anthropic key above empty, then remove the # from
# both lines below and fill them in. MODEL is the model name from your OpenAI
# dashboard. If both keys are set, Anthropic wins.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# MODEL=

# Optional, with Anthropic: use a different Claude model than the default,
# claude-haiku-5-5. Remove the # to use it.
# MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# Optional: if set, the page must send this password. It stops strangers
# spending your AI credit. Mostly useful once the app is online.
# APP_PASSWORD=

# Optional: turns on PostHog analytics. Without a key, nothing is tracked.
# Anything starting NEXT_PUBLIC_ is sent to the browser, so only ever put
# public values in these two.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_...
# Only needed for an EU PostHog project.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com
